WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.734 --> 00:00:01.501
If you're planning to

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.502
watch the upcoming

00:00:02.502 --> 00:00:03.169
Super Bowl,

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:05.905
you'll likely see a few ads about Jesus.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.507
CNN's Tom Foreman looks at

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.676
who is behind the He Gets US campaign

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:11.411
and why some are calling this

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:14.180
a PR stunt for right wing politics.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:17.917
There was this controversial figure.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.085
Everywhere he went,

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.754
people challenged him.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:22.288
The message is stark

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:26.059
arresting and backed by $100 million.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.527
That's how much organizers say

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:29.829
is behind this campaign to market

00:00:29.829 --> 00:00:31.731
Jesus as a patient,

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.633
loving, inclusive cure

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.802
for our divisive times.

00:00:35.802 --> 00:00:38.004
With the tagline He Gets US.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.506
Jason Van der Ground.

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.941
We're trying to unify the American people

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:43.576
around the confounding love

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.111
and forgiveness of Jesus.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.846
The campaign website is filled

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.014
with phrases saying

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:50.016
Jesus called out the toxic

00:00:50.016 --> 00:00:52.018
religious and political systems.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.354
Led the protest against the walls

00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:55.388
that divide us

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.823
and broke the chains

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.658
that held women in bondage.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:00:59.726
Merchandise declares

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:02.228
Jesus was a refugee and an immigrant.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:03.930
At first blush,

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.498
it can all read like a stand

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.001
against radical right wing politics

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:10.103
and related divisiveness.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:12.205
But the campaign pointedly

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:14.941
says this is not an attack on anyone.

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:17.110
It is an outreach to young Americans

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:18.244
whom polls show

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.212
are abandoning

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:21.147
Christianity and other faiths

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.083
at a historic pace.

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:23.583
A lot of times

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.285
when people look at Christianity,

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.320
they see it as much more unfortunate

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.121
of hypocrites.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:30.890
Full, judgmental, kind of discriminatory.

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.059
Ad The fact that he gets us

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:33.660
is funded

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.161
by anonymous donors

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.496
acting through a Kansas

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:37.497
nonprofit

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:40.166
link to staunchly conservative causes.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.869
And it raises alarms for some skeptics,

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.404
such as Chrissie Stroup,

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.672
a former evangelical

00:01:45.672 --> 00:01:47.474
who now reports on religion.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:51.177
I believe he gets his campaign is a PR

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:54.180
effort and website

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.348
strategically developed

00:01:55.348 --> 00:01:56.116
by right

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:57.250
wing evangelicals

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.252
to rope people in with inclusive

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.687
sounding messaging

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:03.156
and get them plugged in to local churches

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.090
that will

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:04.958
eventually teach them

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.092
that to be a Christian means to

00:02:06.092 --> 00:02:07.627
support right wing politics

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:13.500
On top of that, this whole

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.034
big money marketing of Jesus

00:02:15.034 --> 00:02:17.437
just makes some Christians uneasy

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:20.306
so take it how you will that he gets.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.175
His campaign is still moving forward.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.377
They plan to release two new commercials

00:02:24.377 --> 00:02:25.645
during the Super Bowl

00:02:25.645 --> 00:02:26.679
where ad age reports

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.381
some 32nd spots are now

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:31.284
going for $7 million a pop.

